{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310833,"nonce":"9vzKkVc62UfxtHe5KeGUpECsRIc=","title":"FQN-keyed StdlibMapping - Stages 1 and 2a LANDED; what remains is Stage 2b caller cleanup and Stage 3 deletion of the alias closure","message":"Replacing bare-name suffix matching in `compiler/src/stdlib/runtime_mapping.rs`\nwith FQN-keyed lookup, per [[feedback-fqn-first-resolution]].\n\n**LANDED 2026-08-16** (all verified: 183/184 suite with per-test verdicts\nidentical to baseline, 4 e2e suites cold+warm, nue smoke Qwen 15.08 tok/s,\nfrozen snapshot unchanged, cold start 0.29→0.26s):\n- `6f5d8f07` Stage 1: alias index + BTreeMap ranges + class_meta replace 11\n  whole-table scans. `StdlibMapping::builtin()` OnceLock — Cranelift built the\n  whole table PER FUNCTION DECLARED; indexing alone was a 40ms REGRESSION\n  until that was shared.\n- `d19cb25d` `class_names_by_scope` kills the per-member symbol-table scan.\n- `7742a4d4` frozen `mapping_snapshot.txt` (662 lines, canonically named).\n- `a8e9f097` mono-var wrapper dispatch resolves via the table, not\n  `format!(\"{}_{}\", class, method)` — was the rename blocker.\n- `6fb11a12` `TOPLEVEL_STDLIB_CLASSES` one const (two copies had drifted).\n- `7a7ee500` **Stage 2a**: all 73 keys are dotted FQNs; bare-Bytes block\n  deleted; transitional aliases accept every old spelling (both separators,\n  all suffixes); `detect_stdlib_class_from_call` reads the callee's DECLARED\n  RETURN TYPE (survives generic erasure) instead of method-name lists and a\n  first-match-wins scan over all classes; Mutex.lock→MutexGuard moved into\n  `return_class` data; hints canonicalized at producers\n  (`canonical_class_spelling`); `same_class` replaces hand-rolled `_`-suffix\n  compares; extern auto-registration consults builtin+plugins combined.\n\n**USER'S STANDING PUSH (repeated three ways this session): no name lists, no\nguesses at call sites — declarations and metadata are the source of truth.**\nMethod return classes come from signatures; if semantics ever exceed\nsignatures, use Haxe metadata, not compiler-side lists.\n\n**TRAP (cost a crash + a build cycle):** canonicalizing hint producers makes\npreviously-unreachable POISON ENTRIES reachable. Typed-file extern\nauto-registration (`register_extern_methods_from_typed_file`,\ncompilation.rs~8420) guessed bare-name runtime symbols for bodyless\nno-@:native extern methods; the entry keyed by qualified name was never hit\nuntil hints became qualified — then `can't resolve symbol dequantView` at JIT\nlink in nue's KvCacheQ8. Fix: the skip logic consults\n`build_combined_mapping()` (builtin + loaded dylibs), not just builtin.\nThe dylib descriptor is the authority for its own symbols.\n\n**STAGE 2b LANDED `4ef2725d` (2026-08-16/17).** All underscore builders in\nlookups.rs/resolved_method/static_receiver/boxing/module/stdlib_static now\nemit dotted/canonical; `RAYZOR_STDLIB_ALIAS_LOG` (query paths only — the\nsanctioned resolvers `get_class_static_str`/`same_class` are quiet by design)\nwent 43 → 21 distinct spellings, **all single-candidate except `Socket`**.\n`RAYZOR_STDLIB_ALIAS_TRAP=\u003cspelling\u003e` prints a backtrace at the producer —\nuse the DEBUG binary, release frames inline away. hdll `haxe_name` now\nrsplits on the last dot. Extern auto-registration keys dotted-only (was\n`::`+dotted+underscore, tripling keys). **haxe.io.Bytes is no longer a key**\n— it is a declared TYPEDEF_ALIAS of rayzor.Bytes in `rebuild_index` (the two\nkeys had DIVERGING method sets: subU64 under one, address under the other).\n\n**PTR BUG FIXED `a3ed3e74`**: variants re-registered as `deref$4`-style\nmethod spellings (unreachable from Haxe), defaults restored, and `register`\nnow PANICS on duplicate signatures in the builtin table. Real severity\nfound: the pointee-size redirect at `stdlib_runtime.rs:1374` only rewrites\nfrom the DEFAULT names, so while evicted, EVERY un-redirected Ptr.deref\nresolved to the 1-BYTE variant. Decode tok/s A/B deferred — user was running\ngates; correctness verified (identical smoke output, suite verdict-identical,\ne2e cold+warm).\n\n**STAGE 3 LANDED** `e26cbfa3` + `b733c841` (2026-08-17). **Query paths now\nREFUSE any spelling that is not a registered key** — `query_candidates`\npanics naming the spelling, the class it denotes and the query site.\nResolution is confined to `get_class_static_str` (known class) and\n`unique_class_key` (only a simple name survives; refuses to choose between\ncandidates). Alias traffic 43 → 0 across the whole corpus AND nue.\nThe bare-name retry at the end of `get_stdlib_runtime_info_inner` is DELETED\n(it also caused the `Socket` ambiguity). `lower_new` resolves once instead of\ntrying five spellings.\n\n**PROBE (kept, and the way to do this work):** `RAYZOR_STDLIB_ALIAS_LOG=1`\nlogs `spelling -\u003e [classes]  from \u003cfile:line\u003e` — each line names its OWN\nproducer, so ONE corpus run lists every caller left to fix, deduped. Use a\nDEBUG binary (release inlines the frames away). This replaced one-at-a-time\nbacktrace trapping and was far faster.\n\n**PLUGINS DECLARE DOTTED NAMES.** nue-plugins declared\n`nue_transformer_KvCacheQ8` and rayzor-tensors `rayzor_ds_Tensor` — second\nkeys for classes the compiler also knows by their real FQNs, i.e. one class\nwith two method sets. Fixed in the PLUGIN SOURCES (not by guessing in the\ncompiler). `compiler_plugin::normalize_class_name` rewrites only `::` → `.`;\nan underscore is legal IN a class name (`_Internal`), so it is left alone.\nTRAP: after `sed`-ing a plugin's lib.rs, `cargo build -p \u003cplugin\u003e` may not\nnotice — `touch` the file, then confirm with\n`strings target/release/lib\u003cplugin\u003e.dylib | grep \u003cold-key\u003e`.\n\n**STATIC_SEARCH FIXED** `a372b774`: a bare static call resolved by scanning\nevery class for a matching static (first match = whichever class SORTS\nearliest) now asks the method symbol's declared owner. No owner ⇒ the method\nname alone, and only when it identifies a single binding\n(`find_unique_static_by_name_and_params`: entries agreeing on the runtime\nsymbol are one binding under several names; disagreement ⇒ unresolved, never\na pick). **This was the last bare-name scan.**\n\n**MEASUREMENT STATUS:** Qwen2.5-0.5B-Q6_K decode at HEAD ≈ **50-67 tok/s over\n10 runs (mean ~59, stddev ~6 ≈ 11%)** — the box was under load (1-min avg\n6-8, 15-min 17). That spread is far above the stddev≈1 contamination\nthreshold, so the Ptr-fix decode A/B is STILL UNMEASURED; do not infer one\nfrom these. To do it honestly: revert ONLY the Ptr hunk on top of HEAD (not\ncheckout a3ed3e74^, whose tree differs in 5 other commits), interleave, quiet\nbox. Fast measurement path: `rayzor run llama-chat.rzb --` (prebuilt bundle,\nno compile).\n\n**REMAINING (optional):**\n- `ClassKey` newtype would make the key-only contract a TYPE instead of a\n  runtime panic. Optional: traffic is zero and the panic guards it.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `project_fqn_keyed_stdlib_mapping` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}